# EVERY EXTERN SEAT WHOSE TEXT ENDS AT A TERMINATOR, and the door that
# guards it. A `string` crossing to C means a PREFIX of itself wherever
# the callee stops at the first NUL, so these are the rows where a
# holed value silently means something else — `env("PATH\0/junk")`
# reading PATH.
#
# THE FACT IS DERIVED, NOT KEPT: `make externs` reads every C body we
# own and answers which of them hand an extern's text to a call that
# ends at a terminator. This file records what that answer IS, so the
# day a C body gains a `getenv` its row shows up here as unrecorded
# rather than joining the set in silence.
#
# THE DOOR IS NOT A SPELLING AND NOT AT THE CALL SITE. A guard sits at
# a package's PUBLIC ENTRY and the rows below it are reached only
# through it, so `which` and `search_path` handing text straight to C
# is correct — the question is whether a public verb can reach one of
# these without passing a door, which is a call-graph question the
# compiler answers and no grep does (avra-dtdp). The doors are named
# here so that question has a starting point rather than a search.
#
# row                             door (the public entry that guards)
avra_debug                        none — reads AVRA_DEBUG, never a program's text
avra_ffi_open                     @std/avrac: the compiler's own manifest paths
avra_ffi_symbol                   @std/avrac: the compiler's own symbol names
avra_ffi_symbol_in                @std/avrac: the compiler's own symbol names
avra_host_env                     @std/io `env` (nul_at), @std/process `tool`, `tool_from_env`, `Env.get` (nul_at)
avra_host_is_dir                  @std/avrac: the workspace host's own paths
avra_io_env_set                   @std/io `env` (nul_at)
avra_io_kind                      @std/io `one_path` (an inline NUL scan)
avra_io_list                      @std/io `one_path`
avra_io_mkdir                     @std/io `one_path`
avra_io_open                      @std/io `one_path`
avra_io_open_append               @std/io `one_path`
avra_io_open_beneath              @std/io `one_path`, on the root and the path both
avra_io_stamp                     @std/io `one_path`
avra_io_remove                    @std/io `one_path`
avra_io_temp                      @std/io `one_path`
avra_io_watch_add                 @std/io `one_path`
avra_llvm_add_function            backend: the compiler's own symbol names
avra_llvm_emit_object_later_targeted       backend: the compiler's own output paths
avra_llvm_print_module_to_file    backend: the compiler's own output paths
avra_llvm_write_bitcode_to_file   backend: the compiler's own output paths
avra_net_lookup                   @std/net `Resolver.resolve` (names_a_host)
avra_proc_executable              @std/process `tool` (nul_at)
avra_proc_spawn                   @std/process `tool` (nul_at)
avra_qtrace                       none — reads AVRA_QTRACE, never a program's text
avra_selfhost_file_exists         @std/avrac: the compiler's own source paths
avra_selfhost_read_file           @std/avrac: the compiler's own source paths
